Fix all of the following issues in `apps/orchestrator/src/projects/project-store.ts`:

## Fix 1 — Critical: deleteProject must remove the whole directory
`unlink` only removes `project.json`, leaving GBs of media files on disk forever. Use `rm` (recursive) instead:

```typescript
import { readFile, writeFile, readdir, mkdir, rm, rename } from "node:fs/promises";
// ...
async deleteProject(id: string): Promise<boolean> {
  const dir = this.projectDir(id);
  if (!existsSync(dir)) return false;
  await rm(dir, { recursive: true, force: true });
  return true;
}
```

## Fix 2 — Important: atomic writes via write-then-rename
`writeFile` truncates in place — a crash mid-write corrupts `project.json` permanently. Write to a `.tmp` then `rename`:

```typescript
async saveProject(project: Project): Promise<Project> {
  await this.ensureProjectDir(project.id);
  const updated: Project = { ...project, modifiedAt: Date.now() };
  const finalPath = this.projectJsonPath(project.id);
  const tmpPath = finalPath + ".tmp";
  await writeFile(tmpPath, JSON.stringify(updated, null, 2), "utf-8");
  await rename(tmpPath, finalPath);
  return updated;
}
```

Note `saveProject` now returns `Promise<Project>` (the updated object with the correct `modifiedAt`).

## Fix 3 — Important: callers must use the returned updated project
Update `createProject` and `renameProject` to use the return value of `saveProject`:

```typescript
async createProject(name: string, settings?: Partial<ProjectSettings>): Promise<Project> {
  const id = crypto.randomUUID();
  const project = defaultProject({ id, name, settings });
  return this.saveProject(project);  // return updated with persisted modifiedAt
}

async renameProject(id: string, name: string): Promise<Project | null> {
  const project = await this.loadProject(id);
  if (!project) return null;
  const renamed: Project = { ...project, name };
  return this.saveProject(renamed);  // return updated with persisted modifiedAt
}
```

## Fix 4 — Important: parallel reads in listProjects
The serial `for-of` with `await` inside is slow for many projects. Replace with `Promise.all`:

```typescript
async listProjects(): Promise<ProjectSummary[]> {
  await mkdir(this.projectsDir, { recursive: true });
  const entries = await readdir(this.projectsDir, { withFileTypes: true });
  const dirs = entries.filter((e) => e.isDirectory());
  const summaries = (await Promise.all(
    dirs.map(async (dir) => {
      const jsonPath = join(this.projectsDir, dir.name, "project.json");
      try {
        const raw = await readFile(jsonPath, "utf-8");
        const p = JSON.parse(raw) as Project;
        return { id: p.id, name: p.name, createdAt: p.createdAt, modifiedAt: p.modifiedAt } as ProjectSummary;
      } catch {
        return null;
      }
    }),
  )).filter((s): s is ProjectSummary => s !== null);
  return summaries.sort((a, b) => b.modifiedAt - a.modifiedAt);
}
```
(The `existsSync` check inside the loop is no longer needed — try/catch handles ENOENT.)

