## Summary

**Root cause:** `InspectorPanel.tsx` used `inspectedAsset` from the ui-store directly. When `replaceMediaAsset` updated the `MediaItem` in the project-store (new object with new `name`, `blob`, waveform, etc.), the ui-store's `inspectedAsset` still held the **stale object reference**. The inspector header, file info tab, and audio tab all received this stale `item` prop, so the filename never updated in the UI after linking a file.

**Fix** (1 file, 7 lines changed):

`apps/web/src/components/editor/InspectorPanel.tsx` line 116 — replaced the simple fallback:
```tsx
const effectiveInspectedAsset = inspectedAsset ?? selectedClipMediaItem;
```
with a `useMemo` that always re-derives a fresh reference from the project store whenever `project.modifiedAt` changes:
```tsx
const effectiveInspectedAsset = useMemo(() => {
    const base = inspectedAsset ?? selectedClipMediaItem;
    if (!base) return null;
    return getMediaItem(base.id) ?? base;
}, [inspectedAsset, selectedClipMediaItem, getMediaItem, project.modifiedAt]);
```

